{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.TwMul","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwMul","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.TwBasisField"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.σ_mul_Tw_of_not_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.σ_mul_Tw_of_not_lt","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwMul.lean#L120-L126","doc":"The **down** case on its own: when the length drops, the quadratic\nrelation's coefficients appear. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.σ_mul_Tw_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.σ_mul_Tw_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwMul.lean#L114-L118","doc":"The **up** case on its own: when the length goes up, no coefficients. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.σ_mul_Tw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.σ_mul_Tw","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwMul.lean#L95-L112","doc":"**The multiplication table of `H_n(q)` on its own basis.**  Left\nmultiplication by a generator is exactly the operator `Rs i` that built the\nbasis in the first place — so the *down* case, where the `(q-1)` and `q`\ncoefficients appear, comes for free from `rsFun`.\n\nThis is the statement the Gram determinant needs: it is the whole structure\nconstant table, up and down cases together, in one identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.Tw_mul_Tw","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.Tw_mul_Tw","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwMul.lean#L77-L93","doc":"**The multiplication rule for the basis.**  When the lengths add,\n`T_v · T_w = T_{wv}` — note the order, forced by the handedness of\n`orbitMap` (see the module docstring). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.Tw_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.Tw_one","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwMul.lean#L67-L75","doc":"**`T_1 = 1`.**  The chosen reduced word for the identity is forced to be\nempty, since a reduced word has the length of its product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.toEnd_TwOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.toEnd_TwOf","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwMul.lean#L62-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.toEnd_foldl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.toEnd_foldl","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwMul.lean#L49-L60","doc":"The word product acts as the word acts, on any vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.orbitMap_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.TwBasis.orbitMap_mul","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/TwMul.lean#L43-L47","doc":"`orbitMap` turns a product into the left factor acting on the right\nfactor's orbit — the right factor acts first. ","signatureChunk":0}]}